      ******************************************************************
      *
      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COUSR02C UPDATE USER ADMIN TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COUSR02C's update-user CICS transaction by mocking
      *  ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS API: the
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator emits in
      *  place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND MAP, READ
      *  DATASET ... UPDATE, REWRITE DATASET, XCTL, RETURN).  The
      *  DFHEI1 entry point is the single ABI seam between the
      *  production COBOL program and the CICS runtime; mocking it
      *  intercepts every CICS service call without requiring a live
      *  CICS region.
      *
      *  Internal COUSR02C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Every
      *  TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM
      *  so the testsuite asserts against side effects of actual
      *  production-code execution (per the user directive in AAP
      *  Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser supports the mock-types
      *  CALL, PARA, PARAGRAPH, and SECTION (verified against the
      *  Keywords class in cobol-check-0.2.16.jar).  At link time on
      *  z/OS the CICS translator (DFHECP1$) rewrites every
      *      EXEC CICS <verb> ... END-EXEC.
      *  into a sequence whose terminal statement is
      *      CALL 'DFHEI1' USING <command-block> ...
      *  so MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is the equivalent intercept point.
      *  Off-platform (GnuCOBOL on Linux) the same mock applies once
      *  the CICS translator runs as a precompile pass; until that
      *  pass exists in this repository the production EXEC CICS
      *  verbs reach the linker as-is, the merged binary fails to
      *  compile (a known infrastructure gap covered by AAP Section
      *  6.6.3.1's documented "manual testing only" baseline), and
      *  the mock simply registers without firing.  The testsuite
      *  itself is forward-compatible: when a CICS translator pass
      *  is added, the same .cut file exercises every CICS boundary
      *  through this mock.
      *
      *  Mock placement rule
      *  -------------------
      *  Each MOCK is declared INSIDE its corresponding TESTCASE
      *  block (after the TESTCASE keyword) so the cobol-check parser
      *  binds the mock's Local scope to the CURRENT testcase name.
      *  This guarantees that the matching VERIFY clause inside the
      *  same testcase resolves to the testcase-specific Local mock
      *  with the testcase-specific mock body.  This mirrors the
      *  exemplar pattern in tests/cobol-check/COUSR03C.cut and
      *  tests/cobol-check/CBSTM03A.cut.
      *
      *  Schema dependencies (STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl)
      *  -----------------------------------------------------
      *  The file_schema for this testsuite names two internal
      *  imports:
      *
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy -- 01-level EXTERNAL
      *        working-storage group used by the CEE3ABD and DFHEI1
      *        link-time stubs to publish abend / unmocked-CICS
      *        flags to the testsuite.
      *
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl -- standalone DFHEI1 PROGRAM-ID
      *        compiled into a .so module so that any unmocked
      *        EXEC CICS verb that survives the off-platform compile
      *        resolves at load time (CICS NOT-AUTH 27).
      *
      *  Both stubs are linked at TEST-RUN time by the runner script
      *  tests/cobol-check/scripts/linux_gnucobol_run_tests, which
      *  pre-compiles `tests/stubs/CEEDAYS.cbl`, `tests/stubs/
      *  CEE3ABD.cbl`, and `tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl` as .so modules
      *  in the merged-binary directory and points COB_LIBRARY_PATH
      *  at that directory before invoking cobcrun.  The testsuite
      *  itself does NOT contain `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.` because
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser only recognizes the
      *  keywords TESTSUITE, TESTCASE, MOCK, EXPECT, VERIFY,
      *  BEFORE-EACH, AFTER-EACH, END-BEFORE, END-AFTER, END-MOCK,
      *  CALL, PARA, PARAGRAPH, SECTION (and assertion connectors
      *  TO BE / TO EQUAL / HAPPENED / TIMES / AT LEAST / etc).  A
      *  bare COPY at file scope is parsed as a fieldname token and
      *  triggers a "Unexpected token" SYNTAX ERROR that aborts
      *  cobol-check before it can merge the testsuite into the
      *  production source.  COPY directives are recognized only
      *  inside MOCK ... END-MOCK bodies (where they splice into
      *  the procedure-division mock paragraph) and inside the
      *  production source itself (where the cobol-check
      *  CopybookExpander expands them via application.copybook.
      *  directory).  Adding STUB-ABEND-STATE to WORKING-STORAGE of
      *  the merged binary therefore requires either (a) a small
      *  modification to the production program (out of scope per
      *  AAP Section 0.8.2) or (b) an upgrade of cobol-check to a
      *  release that supports file-scope COPY.  Neither is in
      *  scope for this work; the runtime stubs satisfy the
      *  link-time requirements without WS access from the .cut
      *  file, and the COUSR03C exemplar (the canonical pattern
      *  per AAP Section 0.4.3 and the user prompt) follows the
      *  same omission.  The stubs continue to provide their
      *  intended runtime safety (DFHEI1 NOT-AUTH fallback,
      *  CEE3ABD GOBACK-with-flag) regardless of whether the
      *  testsuite can read the EXTERNAL state.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN with CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
      *          = SPACES; production substitutes the default
      *          'COSGN00C' target, captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields,
      *          and issues XCTL.
      *    TC2 - PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS; production resets
      *          USRIDINL to -1 and clears USRIDINI, FNAMEI, LNAMEI,
      *          PASSWDI, USRTYPEI, and WS-MESSAGE to SPACES.  The
      *          PASSWDI clear is unique to COUSR02C: COUSR03C
      *          (the delete-user transaction) does not maintain a
      *          password field on the BMS map, so this testcase
      *          exercises a production behavior absent from the
      *          sister DELETE program.  No CICS verbs; purely
      *          WORKING-STORAGE side effects.
      *    TC3 - PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with USRIDINI = SPACES;
      *          production EVALUATE TRUE matches the empty-user-id
      *          branch, sets WS-ERR-FLG ON, and short-circuits
      *          before any READ DATASET dispatches.
      *    TC4 - PERFORM UPDATE-USER-INFO with USRIDINI / FNAMEI /
      *          LNAMEI populated, PASSWDI = SPACES, USRTYPEI = 'A';
      *          production EVALUATE TRUE walks past the first three
      *          WHEN clauses, matches the WHEN PASSWDI = SPACES OR
      *          LOW-VALUES branch (line 198), sets WS-ERR-FLG ON,
      *          MOVE -1 TO PASSWDL, and short-circuits before any
      *          READ DATASET / REWRITE dispatches.  This branch is
      *          unique to COUSR02C because COUSR03C (delete-user)
      *          does not edit a password.
      *    TC5 - PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN; production performs
      *          INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS first (clearing the BMS map
      *          including PASSWDI) and then SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN.
      *          The test asserts the INITIALIZE side effects
      *          observable in WORKING-STORAGE, including the
      *          PASSWDI clear that distinguishes COUSR02C from
      *          its sister DELETE/LIST programs.
      *
      *  Test user
      *  ---------
      *  Per AAP Section 0.10.2, only ADMIN001 / ADMIN role is
      *  permitted in the COUSR02C testsuite (this transaction is
      *  admin-gated upstream by COADM01C; non-admin access is
      *  filtered before the user reaches COUSR02C, so the program
      *  itself does not implement role-based authorization and
      *  therefore has no test surface for a "non-admin attempting
      *  access rejected" case as the AAP TC4 stub would imply --
      *  the rejection occurs in COADM01C, not COUSR02C, so the
      *  TC4 slot is repurposed to the unique-to-COUSR02C PASSWORD
      *  validation branch described above).
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 -- user directive on test structure
      *    AAP Section 0.5.1  -- file-by-file plan for COUSR02C
      *    AAP Section 0.10.2 -- ADMIN001 / ADMIN test user
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 143-172 (PROCESS-ENTER-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 177-245 (UPDATE-USER-INFO)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 250-261 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 320-353 (READ-USER-SEC-FILE)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 358-390 (UPDATE-USER-SEC-FILE)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 395-398 (CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl lines 403-411 (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy            (SEC-USER-DATA layout)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COUSR02.CPY         (COUSR2AI / COUSR2AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl          (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR03C.cut  (canonical exemplar)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'COUSR02C UPDATE USER ADMIN TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the application working-storage
      *  fields and shared structures the production code reads or
      *  writes:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        - WS-PGMNAME, WS-TRANID, WS-MESSAGE,
      *                          WS-USRSEC-FILE, WS-ERR-FLG, WS-RESP-CD,
      *                          WS-REAS-CD, WS-USR-MODIFIED.  After
      *                          INITIALIZE re-applies VALUE clauses,
      *                          WS-PGMNAME = 'COUSR02C', WS-TRANID =
      *                          'CU02', and WS-ERR-FLG = 'N' (per
      *                          production lines 36-42).
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   - whole COCOM01Y group plus the
      *                          CDEMO-CU02-INFO extension fields
      *                          (CDEMO-CU02-USRID-FIRST,
      *                           CDEMO-CU02-USRID-LAST,
      *                           CDEMO-CU02-PAGE-NUM,
      *                           CDEMO-CU02-NEXT-PAGE-FLG,
      *                           CDEMO-CU02-USR-SEL-FLG,
      *                           CDEMO-CU02-USR-SELECTED).  Note
      *                          the CU02 suffix vs. COUSR03C's CU03
      *                          suffix -- different CICS
      *                          transactions own different
      *                          extension blocks of the shared
      *                          COMMAREA.
      *    SEC-USER-DATA       - CSUSR01Y group (SEC-USR-ID,
      *                          SEC-USR-FNAME, SEC-USR-LNAME,
      *                          SEC-USR-PWD, SEC-USR-TYPE,
      *                          SEC-USR-FILLER)
      *    COUSR2AI            - BMS input map (USRIDINI, FNAMEI,
      *                          LNAMEI, PASSWDI, USRTYPEI, ERRMSGI
      *                          ...).  Note PASSWDI is unique to
      *                          COUSR02C (the update transaction
      *                          edits passwords) and is absent
      *                          from COUSR03C's COUSR3AI map.
      *    RETURN-CODE         - implicit special register reset for
      *                          deterministic post-test inspection
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  ADMIN001 admin-role identity (the only test user permitted
      *  by AAP Section 0.10.2 for this transaction) so each TESTCASE
      *  starts from the routed-by-COADM01C state that production
      *  COUSR02C expects.  CDEMO-FROM-* fields default to the
      *  upstream admin menu so the RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN paragraph
      *  has a non-empty origin to reflect back into the COMMAREA.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE SEC-USER-DATA
            INITIALIZE COUSR2AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'ADMIN001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'A'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COADM01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CA00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 250-261).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3
      *  branch (production lines 111-119), the WHEN DFHPF12 branch
      *  (production lines 124-126), and the EIBCALEN = 0 initial-
      *  entry branch (production lines 90-92).
      *
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 252)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 253)
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 255)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 256)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 257)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 258)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 259)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 260)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 261)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC1 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in
      *                       BEFORE-EACH; INITIALIZE on a PIC X
      *                       group fills with spaces, satisfying
      *                       the WHEN OR SPACES half of the
      *                       line-252 IF).
      *    CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COADM01C' (BEFORE-EACH default;
      *                       will be overwritten by line-256
      *                       production MOVE -- the test asserts
      *                       the SIDE EFFECT)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 253 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side
      *                 effect, does NOT recompute or paraphrase
      *                 the IF logic)
      *    'COUSR02C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 36 (PIC X(08) VALUE 'COUSR02C'); MOVE'd
      *                 to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 256
      *    'CU02'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 37 (PIC X(04) VALUE 'CU02'); MOVE'd to
      *                 CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 255
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR02C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COUSR02C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CU02'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears the map and message
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (production lines 403-411).
      *  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM
      *  statements; it is the cleanest test target in COUSR02C.
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    MOVE -1     TO USRIDINL OF COUSR2AI                (line 405)
      *    MOVE SPACES TO USRIDINI OF COUSR2AI                (line 406)
      *                   FNAMEI   OF COUSR2AI                (line 407)
      *                   LNAMEI   OF COUSR2AI                (line 408)
      *                   PASSWDI  OF COUSR2AI                (line 409)
      *                   USRTYPEI OF COUSR2AI                (line 410)
      *                   WS-MESSAGE.                         (line 411)
      *
      *  COUSR02C-unique behavior: line 409 clears PASSWDI -- a
      *  field that does NOT exist in COUSR03C's INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *  FIELDS (lines 351-356 of COUSR03C.cbl), because the delete-
      *  user transaction does not edit passwords.  This testcase
      *  asserts the PASSWDI clear explicitly so a regression that
      *  drops line 409 from the production source would be caught.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude (after BEFORE-EACH
      *  zeroes the structures): seed USRIDINI / FNAMEI / LNAMEI /
      *  PASSWDI / USRTYPEI / WS-MESSAGE with non-empty markers so
      *  the test proves the production MOVE TO SPACES actually
      *  overwrites them.  Without these seeds the BEFORE-EACH
      *  initial state would already be SPACES and the test would
      *  not distinguish the production paragraph's effect from
      *  baseline.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES     - production literal MOVE'd by lines 406-411;
      *                 the test asserts the side effect (does NOT
      *                 reimplement the MOVE)
      *
      *  A MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so the testcase can also
      *  ASSERT (via VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0 TIMES) the production
      *  invariant that INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS NEVER reaches a CICS
      *  service call.  This is a meaningful production-behavior
      *  assertion: a regression that introduces an EXEC CICS verb
      *  inside this paragraph would inflate the mock count and
      *  fail the VERIFY clause.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR02C INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears six fields'
            MOVE 'OLDUSER ' TO USRIDINI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'OLDFNAME            ' TO FNAMEI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'OLDLNAME            ' TO LNAMEI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'OLDPASS ' TO PASSWDI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'X' TO USRTYPEI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT USRIDINI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT FNAMEI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT LNAMEI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT PASSWDI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT USRTYPEI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty user ID
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 143-172) with
      *  USRIDINI cleared by INITIALIZE COUSR2AI in BEFORE-EACH (so
      *  the field holds LOW-VALUES, which the production EVALUATE
      *  TRUE WHEN clause matches alongside SPACES).  The production
      *  EVALUATE block executes:
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN USRIDINI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 146)
      *            MOVE 'Y' TO WS-ERR-FLG                  (line 147)
      *            MOVE 'User ID can NOT be empty...' TO WS-MESSAGE
      *                                                    (line 148-9)
      *            MOVE -1  TO USRIDINL                    (line 150)
      *            PERFORM SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN              (line 151)
      *        WHEN OTHER
      *            MOVE -1 TO USRIDINL                     (line 153)
      *            CONTINUE                                (line 154)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                    (line 155)
      *
      *  After the EVALUATE, the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 157
      *  is FALSE because production set WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y', so the
      *  paragraph short-circuits without ever issuing READ-USER-SEC-
      *  FILE.  This is the production-mandated invariant: validation
      *  failures gate CICS / VSAM I/O.
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN's
      *  EXEC CICS SEND can be intercepted (after CICS translator
      *  rewrites it to CALL 'DFHEI1') without spawning any real
      *  3270 traffic; the mock body is CONTINUE so the production
      *  flow returns to PROCESS-ENTER-KEY without side effects.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 147 (test
      *          asserts the side effect, does NOT recompute or
      *          paraphrase the EVALUATE logic)
      *    -1  - USRIDINL flipped by production line 150 (negative
      *          length signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR02C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty user ID'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT USRIDINL OF COUSR2AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- UPDATE-USER-INFO rejects empty PASSWORD
      *
      *  Drives UPDATE-USER-INFO (production lines 177-245) along
      *  the COUSR02C-unique PASSWORD validation branch.  COUSR03C
      *  (delete-user) does not edit passwords; this branch
      *  therefore exists ONLY in COUSR02C and forms a key piece of
      *  differential behavior the testsuite must exercise.
      *
      *  The paragraph's EVALUATE block executes (production
      *  lines 179-213):
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN USRIDINI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 180)
      *            ... (USRIDINI is populated; FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN FNAMEI   = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 186)
      *            ... (FNAMEI is populated; FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN LNAMEI   = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 192)
      *            ... (LNAMEI is populated; FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN PASSWDI  = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 198)
      *            MOVE 'Y' TO WS-ERR-FLG                  (line 199)
      *            MOVE 'Password can NOT be empty...' TO WS-MESSAGE
      *                                                    (line 200-1)
      *            MOVE -1  TO PASSWDL                     (line 202)
      *            PERFORM SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN              (line 203)
      *        WHEN USRTYPEI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 204)
      *            ... (already short-circuited; not reached)
      *        WHEN OTHER
      *            ... (not reached)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                    (line 213)
      *
      *  After the EVALUATE, the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 215
      *  is FALSE because production set WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y' on line
      *  199, so the paragraph short-circuits without ever issuing
      *  READ-USER-SEC-FILE or UPDATE-USER-SEC-FILE.  The READ
      *  + REWRITE pair is the canonical CICS happy-path under z/OS;
      *  this validation guard prevents reaching it on bad input,
      *  matching the AAP Section 0.4.1 directive that "validation
      *  failures gate CICS / VSAM I/O."
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC4 prelude:
      *    USRIDINI = 'ADMIN001'  (8 bytes, full)
      *    FNAMEI   = 'Admin Tester        '  (20 bytes, padded)
      *    LNAMEI   = 'User Account        '  (20 bytes, padded)
      *    PASSWDI  = SPACES                (8 bytes, all spaces --
      *                                      the production MATCH
      *                                      target on line 198)
      *    USRTYPEI = 'A'                   (admin role)
      *
      *  These seeds satisfy the WHEN clauses on lines 180, 186, and
      *  192 (none match), then matches on line 198, then never
      *  reaches line 204.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 199 (test
      *          asserts the side effect, does NOT recompute or
      *          paraphrase the EVALUATE logic)
      *    -1  - PASSWDL flipped by production line 202 (negative
      *          length signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer for
      *          the password field).  This is the assertion that
      *          distinguishes COUSR02C from sister CRUD programs.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR02C UPDATE-USER-INFO rejects empty PASSWORD'
            MOVE 'ADMIN001' TO USRIDINI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'Admin Tester        ' TO FNAMEI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'User Account        ' TO LNAMEI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE SPACES TO PASSWDI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'A' TO USRTYPEI OF COUSR2AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM UPDATE-USER-INFO
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT PASSWDL OF COUSR2AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE + SEND
      *
      *  Drives CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN (production lines 395-398).
      *  The paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF4
      *  branch (production lines 120-121) and executes:
      *
      *    PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS.            (line 397)
      *    PERFORM SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN.               (line 398)
      *
      *  PERFORM 1: INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (lines 403-411) -- the
      *  same paragraph TC2 covers in isolation.  Here we assert
      *  the SAME side effects manifest when the orchestrator runs
      *  end-to-end, proving the orchestrator does not bypass or
      *  short-circuit its inner PERFORMs.  Because INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *  FIELDS clears PASSWDI (line 409) -- the COUSR02C-unique
      *  field -- this testcase also asserts that PASSWDI is cleared
      *  by the orchestrator's first PERFORM, complementing the TC2
      *  isolated coverage with end-to-end coverage.
      *
      *  PERFORM 2: SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN (lines 266-278) -- performs
      *  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO and then issues EXEC CICS SEND MAP.
      *  The mock intercepts the SEND verb (after CICS translator
      *  rewrites it to CALL 'DFHEI1') so no 3270 traffic is
      *  generated.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC5 prelude: seed USRIDINI,
      *  PASSWDI, and WS-MESSAGE so the test proves that CLEAR-
      *  CURRENT-SCREEN's first PERFORM (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *  reaches and executes its MOVE-TO-SPACES statements
      *  including the PASSWDI clear.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *             FIELDS lines 406-411; the test asserts the side
      *             effect (does NOT reimplement the MOVE)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR02C CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN clears WS-MSG PASSWDI'
            MOVE 'OLDUSER ' TO USRIDINI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'OLDPASS ' TO PASSWDI OF COUSR2AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN
            EXPECT USRIDINI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT PASSWDI OF COUSR2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COUSR02C UPDATE USER ADMIN TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************
